WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.168
-Now, here's how it works.

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.502
We'll each be served
a gourmet three-course meal,

00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:06.806
but each dish contains
one unusual secret ingredient.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.709
And it's our job to figure out
what that ingredient is.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:12.211
Higgins,
what is the first course?

00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:15.648
-Well, to start, it's
our Baja pineapple margarita,

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:18.985
made with organic pineapple,
fresh lime juice,

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:21.855
and glass-rested tequila blanco.

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:25.924
But can you guess
the secret ingredient?

00:00:25.924 --> 00:00:27.193
[ Laughs maniacally ]

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:28.962
Bon appétit!
[Mimics echoing]

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:31.130
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.465
-Cheers, okay.
-What is it?

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.266
-Cheers.
-There's an ingredient in there.

00:00:34.266 --> 00:00:35.601
It's --
-Ew.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:38.738
-Oh, I already smelled it.
-Ew.

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:41.374
Ew!
-No, wrong.

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:42.842
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:46.980
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.050
-Mmm.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.718
-I think Jim is going to write
down "fun" for his --

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:53.986
-This is all right, that.

00:00:53.986 --> 00:00:55.387
[ Laughter ]
-What do you think it is?

00:00:55.387 --> 00:00:58.391
Write down your answers.
What could it possibly be?

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.192
Ready? Jennifer,

00:01:00.192 --> 00:01:02.295
what do you think the secret --

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.630
-I think Jennifer
is going to know this.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:05.764
-Pickle juice!

00:01:05.764 --> 00:01:07.766
[ Buzzer, sad tuba plays ]
No.

00:01:07.766 --> 00:01:09.469
Wrong. Sorry.
-I mean...

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.071
-Jimmy?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.239
-Fine, it's fine.
-Jimmy, what do you think

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:14.907
the secret ingredient was,

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:17.243
knowing it's not pickle juice
nor fun.

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.711
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.780
-I wouldn't think
it was pickle juice.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:21.847
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:24.383
-Only a fool would write
"pickle juice"

00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:25.951
Uh, pickle juice.
-Oh!

00:01:25.951 --> 00:01:28.154
[ Buzzer, sad tuba plays ]

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:30.256
Wrong.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.991
Okay, Jim, it's up to you.

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:34.794
-I think it had, like,
a smokey overtone.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.163
I think it's some type of meat,
ham.

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:38.164
-Eh!

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:40.066
[ Buzzer, sad tuba plays ]
-Ham.

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:42.001
It was mustard.
-Ew!

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.570
-Ah, mustard.
Or mut-ard as you say, Jim.

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:46.772
-Yeah, but mustard goes good
with ham.

00:01:46.772 --> 00:01:48.508
-It does.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:49.676
Half point.

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:51.411
-You can't give him
a half point for that.

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:53.079
-Well, guess what? I just did.
-All right.

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:54.947
-For your next course --
-Gosh.

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:56.582
-We have
an autumn harvest chili --

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:57.716
-All right, bring it, bring it.

00:01:57.716 --> 00:01:59.819
-Topped with local
aged cheddar cheese...

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:02.355
-Chili.
-...fried corn tortillas...

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.756
-Yep.
-...and finished with

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:07.627
Italian parsley, But can you
guess the secret ingredient?

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:08.928
Bon appétit!

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:10.897
What is it? It's secret.

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:12.565
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:14.067
Mmm.

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.135
Whoa.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.335
-Get the corn chips
out of the way.

00:02:16.335 --> 00:02:18.304
Because the corn chips will be
a distraction.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.739
-Yeah, they'll mess up
your palate.

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:21.340
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.876
Oh, not bad.
Not good. Not good.

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:24.944
But not bad.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:26.779
-Chili,
and has a secret ingredient.

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:29.282
-Yeah, so the secret ingredient
is not chili.

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:32.017
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.017 --> 00:02:35.054
Nor corn chips
nor fried tortillas.

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:36.555
Are you ready?
-Hold on.

00:02:36.555 --> 00:02:37.690
-No.
-No.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:38.925
[ Laughter ]
-Have some more.

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:41.226
Let it roll over your tongue.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.226 --> 00:02:42.895
-I don't have any idea.
-There's something, I think.

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:44.263
-It's something --
there's something in there

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:46.232
that's secret.
-What is it --

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:48.334
What is it supposed to be?
Sorry.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.536
-It's supposed to be chili.
-Just chili?

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:52.338
-Chili.
-Okay. I mean, I --

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.907
-What doesn't taste chili-like
about it?

00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:57.377
Does it taste too warm
to be "chili"? [chilly]

00:02:57.377 --> 00:03:00.179
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:01.313
Hey.

00:03:01.313 --> 00:03:03.048
-Who goes first?
-Don't look at me like that.

00:03:03.048 --> 00:03:05.318
-Jennifer, you go first, ready.

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:06.919
What do you think
the secret ingredient is?

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:08.087
Corn?
-I mean --

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.288
-No.
[ Buzzer, sad tuba plays ]

00:03:09.288 --> 00:03:10.957
-That is in chili.
-I know. That's why I'm --

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:12.224
-That is in chili.
-I know.

00:03:12.224 --> 00:03:15.027
-What a delightful secret
ingredient.

00:03:15.027 --> 00:03:16.996
-Yeah, the secret ingredient
is beans and meat.

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.231
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:20.566
-All right, Jimmy,
what do you think?

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:21.968
-Oreo cookies.
-Ooh.

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.403
[ Buzzer, sad tuba plays ]
-Oh, wow.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.204
-Ooh.

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:26.839
Not too shabby.
-All right, all right.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.240
-All right, Jim, what
do you think?

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.209
-I really can't spell. But
I tried to spell "chocolate."

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:31.977
-Oh.
-Oh.

00:03:31.977 --> 00:03:33.012
[ Buzzer, sad tuba plays ]

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.713
-Can we be more specific
with "chocolate?"

00:03:34.713 --> 00:03:36.315
-Oh.
-Oh.

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:40.152
-European-ish.
-Lindor balls.

00:03:40.152 --> 00:03:42.221
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:46.259
Don't swear on this show.
Don't swear on this show.

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:48.193
-Ferrero Rocher?
-It's Nutella.

00:03:48.193 --> 00:03:50.329
[ Ding! ]
-A point to Jim!

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:51.164
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Hazelnut.

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:52.598
-Yeah.
-Oh, hazelnut.

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:54.166
-Yeah.
-Gonna do it, right here.

00:03:54.166 --> 00:03:55.501
-Wow, Jim Jefferies, awesome.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.570
-I'm going to call you guys
the hazel nuts.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.272
I have a feeling this one --

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:00.973
I think you're
going to get this one.

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:02.808
-I don't think so.
-Yes, I do.

00:04:02.808 --> 00:04:04.743
It's for dessert.
-I can't believe I've --

00:04:04.743 --> 00:04:06.913
-Southwest southern-Style
mini red velvet cupcake

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:08.714
with buttercream cherry frosting

00:04:08.714 --> 00:04:10.817
and our homemade
rock candy sprinkles.

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:13.719
And the chef recommends eating
the whole thing in one bite.

00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:17.523
This round is worth 10,000
points.

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:19.291
-Right.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.291 --> 00:04:20.426
[ Audience oohs ]

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:23.061
-One bite. Ready?
One, two, three, one!

00:04:23.061 --> 00:04:26.665
[ Audience groaning ]

00:04:26.665 --> 00:04:29.301
Okay.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:29.301 --> 00:04:31.303
♪♪

00:04:31.303 --> 00:04:33.806
-[ Muffled speaking ]

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:35.941
Okay!

00:04:35.941 --> 00:04:40.146
♪♪

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:44.183
Okay, you are writing it down.
There you go.

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:46.519
Doesn't count unless you write
it on the pad.

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:48.421
Okay, is everybody ready?
-Yes.

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:52.424
-Jennifer, what did you say
the secret ingredient was?

00:04:52.424 --> 00:04:54.560
Toothpaste is correct!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.063
♪♪

00:04:57.063 --> 00:05:00.733
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:03.302
Jimmy. Jimmy.

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:07.106
Jimmy, what did you say --
Hey, leave Jim alone.

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:09.175
Jim's got his own --
-It's toothpaste!

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:12.177
[ Buzzer, sad tuba plays ]
-What do you mean no?

00:05:12.177 --> 00:05:13.279
-Yeah, no, yeah.
-Toothpaste.

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:14.480
-Yeah, yes.
-What's that underneath --

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.883
-Then he put --
-I also wrote "toothpaste."

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:18.184
[ Ding! ]

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:21.287
♪♪

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:23.723
-He wrote gravy.

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:24.590
-So you two win.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.993
So we need what, a taste-Off?

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:29.895
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:29.895 --> 00:05:31.964
-We don't have one.
-What, I got -- I got --

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:33.899
-We don't have one, right?
-No, we don't have one.

00:05:33.899 --> 00:05:35.367
-That's --
-What kind of toothpaste

00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:36.502
was that?
-Oh, let's -- let's just --

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:37.803
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Let's try to guess that.

00:05:37.803 --> 00:05:39.305
-What kind of toothpaste?
-All right, what brand name

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:40.606
toothpaste?
-It's the one with the waves.

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:41.840
-Okay, I'll find out.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:43.008
-What's it called?
-No, no, no.

00:05:43.008 --> 00:05:45.410
-Do you know what I mean?
Come on, Jimmy.

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:47.546
-I know.
-You're writing it down.

00:05:47.546 --> 00:05:49.948
No, it's not that. It's
the one that goes like this.

00:05:49.948 --> 00:05:51.150
-No, you think it's that.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.851
[ Laughter ]
Aquafresh?

00:05:52.851 --> 00:05:54.387
-Yes!
-No, no, no.

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:55.955
-I think so.
-This is the tiebreaker.

00:05:55.955 --> 00:05:58.891
What type of -- do you even know
American names of toothpaste?

00:05:58.891 --> 00:05:59.725
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.725 --> 00:06:01.193
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:01.193 --> 00:06:04.597
-One, two, three, reveal.

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:05.698
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:08.167
Jimmy got it. It's Crest.
[ Dinging ]

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:09.401
Oh.

00:06:09.401 --> 00:06:11.637
♪♪

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:15.941
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:15.941 --> 00:06:18.878
-Our thanks to Jennifer Garner,
Jim Jefferies.

